Let's assume that we are cancelling a monster as MB cannot be used to 
cabncel items.

1. I zap a wand of cancellation and supply a direction when asked. The 
wand wasn't empty, one charge is consumed and a cancellation effect is 
tried on a monster in the supplied direction.

2. I cast a spell of cancellation and supply a direction when asked. The 
casting was succesful, some mana is deducted from my reserves and a 
cancellation effect is tried on a monster in the supplied direction.

3. I attack with MB in a dirction of a monster and MB informs that it's 
cancelling the monster. A cancellation effect is tried on a monster in 
the supplied direction.

In cases 1, 2 and 3 I know that a monster is undergoing a cancellation 
attempt.

In cases 1, 2 and 3 no information is given if the cancellation was 
succesful unless there is some visible consequences on cancellation.

In cases 1 and 2 a failure of cancellation produces no information but 
in case 3 there is a message telling that the monster resists.


My question is: How is the case 3 different from cases 1 and 2 to 
justify the difference?

